      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(browser): time out response body reads",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where Browser response body capture could hang past its timeout when Playwright matched the response headers but the response body read never completed.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe response-body path now carries the existing response deadline through the Playwright `response.body()` read instead of clearing the timer after the matching response event. This keeps the existing URL matching and body truncation behavior while preventing a stalled body read from holding the tool call indefinitely.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers and automation that wait for a Browser response body now get a bounded timeout failure instead of a stuck command when the response body never resolves.\n\n## Evidence\n\nCurrent head: `a61c58749b29d211c1c0c67a87ad3e2cf2185cd3`.\n\n- GitHub Actions `Real behavior proof` passed for this head: `node scripts/github/real-behavior-proof-check.mjs` reported `External PR includes problem context and evidence.` Job: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29613181088/job/87992337426\n- GitHub Actions CI passed for this head, including `openclaw/ci-gate`, `check-lint`, `check-test-types`, `check-prod-types`, `check-dependencies`, and `build-artifacts`. CI gate job: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29612782690/job/87992133440\n- The current PR diff is limited to Browser response body handling and focused regression coverage in `extensions/browser/src/browser/pw-tools-core.responses.ts` and `extensions/browser/src/browser/pw-tools-core.responses.test.ts`.",
